# 5. SCOPE OF THE PROJECT

The scope of the project covers the development of a web-based CRM application for organizing customer information and supporting sales management activities.

The system includes user authentication, lead management, sales pipeline monitoring, task management, dashboard analytics, AI-assisted lead scoring, sentiment analysis, email drafting, and a conversational assistant.

The application is designed to help users maintain customer records, monitor sales opportunities, organize follow-up activities, and review important business metrics through a centralized interface. Its AI-assisted functions provide recommendations and analytical information that can support, but do not replace, human decision-making.

The project primarily focuses on CRM operations and sales-related information. Advanced capabilities such as training predictive models on historical conversion data, integrating enterprise communication systems, and deploying organization-wide access controls can be developed as future extensions.

# 6. EXISTING SYSTEM

Existing customer management approaches may rely on spreadsheets, manual record keeping, and separate applications for communication and task tracking. In such environments, customer information and sales activities may not be available through a single interface.

Lead prioritization is frequently based on individual judgment or simple manual rules. This can make it difficult to apply consistent criteria when evaluating a large number of potential customers. Sales reporting and revenue estimation may also require repeated calculations and manual preparation.

Customer feedback and interaction notes may be stored without systematic sentiment analysis. Consequently, identifying customer concerns and deciding which opportunities require additional attention may involve considerable manual effort.

The main limitations of these approaches include fragmented information, repetitive administrative work, inconsistent follow-ups, limited analytical visibility, and difficulties in maintaining an organized sales pipeline.

# 7. PROPOSED SYSTEM

The proposed system provides a centralized web application that integrates customer relationship management with AI-assisted sales analysis.

The application enables authenticated users to maintain lead information, monitor sales stages, manage tasks, and review business performance through a dashboard. The lead-scoring component evaluates selected lead attributes and generates a score and classification according to the implemented rules.

The dashboard presents relevant sales statistics and a weighted revenue forecast. Additional features support customer sentiment analysis, email drafting, and conversational queries about CRM information.

The backend is developed using Node.js and Express.js, while React.js provides the frontend interface. MongoDB stores application records, and Mongoose manages database schemas and queries. Authentication middleware protects relevant backend routes.

